  "facts": [
    {
      "grade": "DOCUMENTED_PLUS_MEASURED",
      "statement": "main_proj is ColumnParallelLinear(15360,5120,gather_output=True,bias=False). Native output is BF16[M,640], TP8 gather layout [8,M,640], Transpose [M,8,640], then full5120D RMSNorm. first_layer.main_proj/main_norm alias the same objects, not separate weights."
    },
    {
      "grade": "MEASURED",
      "statement": "Three target auxiliary states are HC means. Long local rows800/816/834 gather to6400/6528/6672; graph local3 gathers to24. Indexed auxiliary domains24->12,24->24,6672->6668 are positive. Equal row counts do not prove identity row plans or no duplicates."
    },
    {
      "grade": "DOCUMENTED",
      "statement": "_propose invokes combine_hidden_states then set_inputs_first_pass. Active AscendDSparkProposer inherits AscendDflashProposer but overrides the firstpass setter. DFlash base122/132 has zero selected profile hits and cannot be used as the current publisher."
    },
    {
      "grade": "DOCUMENTED_PLUS_MEASURED",
      "statement": "Actual dspark_proposer.py259 has a prefix copy outside any enclosing conditional, copying target_hidden_states[:_dflash_num_context] to the persistent bank prefix; _dflash_num_context is int(cad.query_start_loc_cpu[batch_size]), not inferred from a tensor shape. There are24 positive native TensorMove. All bank-tail/alias/readiness and other copy domains remain separate."
    },
    {
      "grade": "DOCUMENTED",
      "statement": "DSpark309 builds the per-layer context-slot list by selecting _per_group_context_slot_mapping_buffers[gidx] for _layer_group_idx. It is not the DFlash base int32 Tensor indexed as a layer list. Actual group identities/values are unrecorded; equal group index can establish same source bank under stable mapping, not equal shape alone."
    },
    {
      "grade": "DOCUMENTED_PLUS_MEASURED",
      "statement": "Actual DSpark274 calls the input copy/expand metadata kernel per draft attention group;88 native executions are positive. It publishes query/input/position/context-slot/query-slot/token-index outputs, with rejected-token, SAMPLE_FROM_ANCHOR, DCP_SIZE/DCP_RANK/CP_INTERLEAVE_SIZE inputs. Avoiding hidden-state copy does not delete this work."
    },
    {
      "grade": "DOCUMENTED",
      "statement": "Inherited build_model_inputs_first_pass315 passes the bank prefix, context-position-buffer prefix and per-layer slots to the small forwarding wrapper455 and then DSpark295-309. Empty states/None global slots return; empty positions return inside the layer loop. A per-layer None reaches store after its projection."
    },
    {
      "grade": "DOCUMENTED_PLUS_MEASURED",
      "statement": "Each layer uses its own attn.wkv/kv_norm/cache. model.py417 constructs wkv as ReplicatedLinear(dim,head_dim,bias=False),425 constructs RMSNorm(head_dim,eps). Native wkv is BF16[M,5120] x BF16[512,5120] -> BF16[M,512]. Replicated declaration is not a loaded parameter-equality or binary-attestation measurement."
    },
    {
      "grade": "DOCUMENTED_PLUS_MEASURED",
      "statement": "KV BF16 output -> full512D norm BF16 ->448-nope/64-RoPE split -> interleaved rotation -> ViewCopy of original tail view -> concat -> cache scatter. Preserve BF16 boundaries, each512D normalization, layer weights and per-layer caches; do not norm a combined1536D row."
    },
    {
      "grade": "DOCUMENTED_PLUS_MEASURED",
      "statement": "_apply_dsv4_rope calls get_cos_and_sin_dsa(positions) with use_cache=False,layer_names=None. The same source context_positions expression is passed to all loop iterations. Default query freshly indexes every registered applicable config/group and returns proxies; source185/186 produces FP32 lookup results."
    },
    {
      "grade": "DOCUMENTED",
      "statement": "Existing layer_names filters config keys, then still applies registered group/position-map rules. RopeDataProxy string lookup selects the layer configuration/required groups without writing global query buffers. Under stable registry/tables/positions and normal valid names, filtering/hoisting preserves the selected entries, even if layers use different configs."
    },
    {
      "grade": "DOCUMENTED_PLUS_MEASURED",
      "statement": "ComplexExpRotaryEmbedding.forward400 calls torch_npu.npu_rotary_mul(x,cos,sin), with no explicit source cast;402 copies result into original x view. Two Casts per cycle attributed under400 are native lowering, not two .to(BF16) statements. Sharing FP32 lookup does not prove removal of624 internal casts."
    },
    {
      "grade": "DOCUMENTED",
      "statement": "use_cache=True is an existing API that gathers into mutable global runtime/spec buffers, optionally draft_index-1; missing buffers skip entries. It changes alias/capacity/lifetime/readiness requirements and is not interchangeable with the pure default by a flag alone."
    },
    {
      "grade": "DOCUMENTED_PLUS_MEASURED",
      "statement": "For linear 1D slots the current standard cache writer computes valid=s>=0, physical=max(s,0), (physical//block_size,physical%block_size) INT32, masks invalid pairs to-1, then ScatterNdUpdateSk. All312 selected cycles have this path; native cache input shape[17306,128,512] does not prove valid-slot values, allocation size, duplicate-write semantics or spare capacity."
    },
    {
      "grade": "UNKNOWN",
      "statement": "Actual position/row-index/slot values, _layer_group_idx contents, live pointers/aliases, registry config identities, capture bank observers, weight generations, all cross-iteration reuse keys and physical critical-path gain are not recorded by the selected profile/source packets."
    }
